@startuml corpus-gutenberg-strip
' strip_gutenberg_boilerplate: choose the half-open window [start_idx, end_idx) of
' a Gutenberg text file from the first matching START and END marker.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/corpus-gutenberg-strip.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 3 in docs/components/corpus/formats.md, section "Project Gutenberg".
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
  BorderColor #1565C0
}
title strip_gutenberg_boilerplate — carving the book out of the file

rectangle "**pg1342.txt** — the whole file, as read by fs::read_to_string" as file #546E7A {
  rectangle "**front matter + START marker line — discarded**\ntitle page · licence blurb · producer credits\nmarker: *** START OF THE PROJECT GUTENBERG EBOOK ***" as head #90A4AE
  rectangle "**the book — kept**\ntext[start_idx .. end_idx]\n“It is a truth universally acknowledged, that a single man…”" as body #1565C0
  rectangle "**END marker line + back matter — discarded**\nmarker: *** END OF THE PROJECT GUTENBERG EBOOK ***\nlicence · donation appeal · contributor index" as tail #90A4AE
}

rectangle "**Normalizer::default()**\n(all four passes off — a pass-through)" as norm #1565C0
rectangle "**Document**\nid = file stem, leading “pg” stripped (pg1342 ⇒ 1342)\ntitle = file stem · content = normalized text\nsource = Some(path)" as doc #455A64

head -[hidden]down-> body
body -[hidden]down-> tail
body --> norm : text[start_idx .. end_idx].to_string()
norm --> doc

note right of head
  **start_idx** = index just past the newline that ends the
  first matching START marker line, plus the run of
  whitespace that follows it (blank lines are skipped).
end note

note right of tail
  **end_idx** = length of text[..pos].trim_end(), where pos is
  the first matching END marker **searched from start_idx**,
  so a marker quoted inside the front matter cannot truncate
  the book.
end note

note bottom of doc
  **Marker sets** — first match wins, in source order.
  START: "*** START OF THE PROJECT GUTENBERG",
     "*** START OF THIS PROJECT GUTENBERG",
     "***START OF THE PROJECT GUTENBERG",
     "*END*THE SMALL PRINT"  ← the pre-2000 layout
  END: "*** END OF THE PROJECT GUTENBERG",
     "*** END OF THIS PROJECT GUTENBERG",
     "***END OF THE PROJECT GUTENBERG",
     "End of the Project Gutenberg", "End of Project Gutenberg"

  **Fail-safe.** If no marker matches, or the window is empty
  (start_idx ≥ end_idx), the **whole file** is returned rather than
  nothing — so a non-Gutenberg .txt still trains. A document that
  normalises to the empty string is dropped with a log::warn!.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Role |
  |<#546E7A> | the file (corpus I-O) |
  |<#90A4AE> | boilerplate — discarded |
  |<#1565C0> | retained text · normalisation |
  |<#455A64> | emitted Document |
endlegend
@enduml
